import BlogArticle from "../../components/BlogArticle.astro";
---

<BlogArticle
	title="Documents Required for a New PAN Card Application"
	description="Check the documents for a new PAN card application, including proof of identity, address and date of birth for current Indian Form 93 applicants."
	canonicalUrl="https://nsdlphotoresize.com/blogs/documents-for-new-pan/"
	heading="Documents required for a new PAN card application"
	intro="Gather the supporting documents before you start. The exact checklist depends on the applicant and application route, and the current application form is the final authority."
>
	<section class="space-y-3">
		<h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink">First, select the correct application</h2>
		<p>
			Protean’s current guidance says Indian citizens and Indian
			entities must use Forms 93 and 94, respectively, for new PAN
			applications from 1 April 2026. Foreign citizens and entities use
			Forms 95 and 96. UTIITSL also directs new Indian applicants to
			Forms 93 and 94. Do not start a second application if a PAN has
			already been allotted: having or using more than one PAN is
			prohibited.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section class="space-y-3">
		<h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink">Typical documents for an individual applicant</h2>
		<p>
			The current Protean Form 93 list separates evidence into three
			purposes. An accepted document may satisfy one or more purposes;
			check the table on the official form rather than assuming a
			single document covers everything.
		</p>
		<ul class="list-disc space-y-3 pl-6">
			<li><strong>Proof of identity:</strong> examples in the Form 93 list include Aadhaar, an Indian passport, a driving licence, an Elector’s Photo Identity Card, and specified government identity documents.</li>
			<li><strong>Proof of address:</strong> examples include Aadhaar, an Indian passport, a passport of the spouse, a post office passbook, a domicile certificate, and eligible recent utility or financial statements. Some statements have freshness limits, such as three months.</li>
			<li><strong>Proof of date of birth:</strong> examples include an Indian passport, driving licence, voter identity card, a qualifying government photo ID, a pension payment order, marriage certificate, or recognised board certificate/mark sheet.</li>
		</ul>
		<p>
			For an individual born on or after 1 October 2023, Protean’s
			published Form 93 document list says a birth certificate from the
			authorised registrar or municipal authority (or the applicable
			Indian Consulate) is mandatory as date-of-birth proof. Check the
			current document list for your category and submission method.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section class="space-y-3">
		<h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink">Additional material to have ready</h2>
		<p>
			Keep the applicant’s exact name and date-of-birth details
			consistent with the selected proof. The online flow may request
			contact information, an image/signature, declarations, or
			additional documents based on the selected identity
			verification and delivery method. A paper application may have
			different attachment, certification, or original-document
			instructions than an online application.
		</p>
		<p>
			For an entity, do not use the individual Form 93 list. Form 94
			has its own applicant-specific documents, such as entity
			identity/formation and authorised representative details.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section class="space-y-3">
		<h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink">A simple document checklist</h2>
		<ol class="list-decimal space-y-3 pl-6">
			<li>Choose the current form for your applicant type and provider.</li>
			<li>Identify the accepted proof for identity, address, and date of birth separately.</li>
			<li>Check that names, dates, and addresses match the application; review any document validity or recency rule.</li>
			<li>Prepare clear scans or copies in the file format and size requested by the online form, or follow the printed form’s physical-document instructions.</li>
			<li>Keep the acknowledgement or application number after submission so you can follow up.</li>
		</ol>
	</section>

	<p>
		Review <a class="text-link" href="https://tinpan.proteantech.in/services/pan/documents-form_93-form_94.html">Protean’s official Form 93/94 document list</a>,
		<a class="text-link" href="https://tinpan.proteantech.in/services/pan/instructions-form_93-form_94.html">Form 93/94 instructions</a>,
		and the <a class="text-link" href="https://www.pan.utiitsl.com/PAN/newA.html">UTIITSL current application page</a>
		before applying. Requirements can differ by applicant and provider.
	</p>
</BlogArticle>
